ef 17592186045417] [17592186050985 #edb/ref 1027 #edb/ref 17592186048777 #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186050985 #edb/ref 1027 #edb/ref 17592186050643 #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186050985 #edb/ref 1027 #edb/ref 17592186050789 #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186050985 #edb/ref 1028 #edb/ref 17592186115190 #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186050985 #edb/ref 1028 #edb/ref 17592186115191 #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186050985 #edb/ref 1028 #edb/ref 17592186115192 #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186050985 #edb/ref 1028 #edb/ref 17592186115193 #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186050985 #edb/ref 1029 #edb/ref 17592186428296 #edb/ref 17592186045436] [17592186050985 #edb/ref 1029 #edb/ref 17592186428297 #edb/ref 17592186045436] [17592186050985 #edb/ref 1029 #edb/ref 17592186428298 #edb/ref 17592186045436] [17592186050985 #edb/ref 1031 "Differentiating Reciprocal Trigonometric Functions" #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186050985 #edb/ref 1033 1686 #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186050985 #edb/ref 1034 1.789143713939677 #edb/ref 17592186045436] [17592186050985 #edb/ref 1035 #uuid "770e795e-38d4-5b4f-8bd2-bd698bb6794a" #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186096420 #edb/ref 1069 "e-3637" #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186096420 #edb/ref 1071 "Given that $f(x) = \\dfrac{x} {9x^2 + 5x},$ find $f'(x).$" #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186096420 #edb/ref 1072 #uuid "932c9b44-c040-5ae1-84f7-277767c255d4" #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186096420 #edb/ref 1074 "The numerator and denominator are $u(x) = x$ and $v(x) = 9x^2 + 5x,$ respectively. Their derivatives are given by\n\n \n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}{u}^{′}(x) & =1, \\\\ {v}^{′}(x) & =18x+5.\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nApplying the quotient rule, we have\n\n$$\n\\eqalign{\n\t\t\tf'(x) \t& = \\dfrac {u'(x)\\cdot v(x) - u(x) v'(x)} {[v(x)]^2}\\\n\t\t\t\t& = \\dfrac{\\left( 9x^2+5x \\right )\\cdot 1 -x\\cdot \\left( 18x+5 \\right)}{\\left( 9x^2+5x\\right)^2}\\\n\t\t\t\t& = \\dfrac{\\left( 9x^2+5x-18x^2-5x \\right)}{\\left( 9x^2+5x\\right)^2}\\\n\t\t\t\t& = -\\dfrac{9x^2}{\\left( 9x^2+5x\\right)^2}.\n\t\t}\n$$" #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186096421 #edb/ref 1069 "e-3638" #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186096421 #edb/ref 1071 "If $f(x)=\\dfrac{1+\\sin x}{x},$ find $f'(x).$" #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186096421 #edb/ref 1072 #uuid "f804809a-22bf-5ab3-9775-3591d4581797" #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186096421 #edb/ref 1074 "In this case, the expression for $f(x)$ is a quotient $\\dfrac{u(x)}{v(x)}$ with $u(x) = 1+\\sin x$ and $v(x) = x.$ \n\nTherefore, we apply the quotient rule as follows:\n\n$$\n\\eqalign{\nf'(x) & = \\dfrac{u'(x)\\cdot v(x) - u(x)\\cdot v'(x)}{[v(x)]^2}\\\n\t\t         \t& = \\dfrac{(1+\\sin x)'\\cdot (x) -(1+\\sin x)\\cdot (x)'}{x^2}\\\n\t\t\t        & = \\dfrac{\\cos x \\cdot x- (1+\\sin x)\\cdot 1}{x^2}\\\n\t\t\t\t& = \\dfrac{x \\cos x -\\sin x -1}{x^2}\t\t\t\n}\n$$" #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186096422 #edb/ref 1069 "e-3639" #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186096422 #edb/ref 1071 "Given that $y=\\dfrac{1}{3x+7},$ find $\\dfrac{\\textrm{d}y}{\\textrm{d}x}.$" #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186096422 #edb/ref 1072 #uuid "53d435ea-a20f-5216-8020-f36cdf8b7c36" #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186096422 #edb/ref 1074 "Let $u=1$ and $v=3x+7.$ Then\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}\\frac{\\text{d}u}{\\text{d}x} & =0\\,\\text{and}\\,\\frac{\\text{d}v}{\\text{d}x}=3.\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nUsing the quotient rule, we get\n\n$$\n\\eqalign{\n\t\t\t\\dfrac{\\textrm{d}y}{\\textrm{d}x}\t& = \\dfrac{ v\\dfrac{\\textrm{d}u}{\\textrm{d}x}-u\\dfrac{\\textrm{d}v}{\\textrm{d}x}}{v^2}\\\n\t\t\t\t\t\t\t\t\t\t& = \\dfrac{ \\left( 3x+7 \\right ) \\cdot 0 -1\\cdot 3}{\\left( 3x+7\\right)^2}\\\n\t\t\t\t\t\t\t\t\t\t& = -\\dfrac{3}{\\left( 3x+7\\right)^2}.\n\t\t}\n$$" #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186096620 #edb/ref 1037 #edb/ref 17592186048932 #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186096620 #edb/ref 1038 #edb/ref 17592186097024 #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186096620 #edb/ref 1038 #edb/ref 17592186097025 #edb/ref 1759218604541